From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mpl: anneal from an exact placement when annealing finds none

When every annealing run of a cluster placement ends outside its outline
(MPL-0040 at the root, MPL-0008 below it, MPL-0010 for macros inside a
cluster), the exact check settles whether a placement exists, at each
standard cell utilization the annealer tried. If one does, it seeds an
annealer, as a sequence pair and shapes, that keeps to legal states and
improves the wirelength from there (MPL-0083). If none does, the error
carries the proof and the fixes, and says whether the outline is the
core or mpl's own allocation from the parent level.

The annealer headers are exported to the tests for the gtest of this
path: a planted packing that fills its outline exactly, handed to the
annealer as its exact placement, stays inside the outline.

Not upstreamed; retires at the //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.

